    // RAN: Review gate for Sprint 8 judged 2026-11-11 at be3f5ae. Pass 1, the cause against the logs. The cited lines of mwcmbk4j show four refused connects on device A. The backoff ladder reads 3s, 4s, 9s, 22s. The reconnect at 21:16:53 lands 11 seconds after the server was back at 21:16:41. That supports the named cause. The proxy candidate is excluded by the 200 second probe, the server candidate by 36 published changes. The 503 slow retry and the idle poll appear in no log. Pass 2, the fix. The owner accepted the latency as a risk (st019). The sprint documents the behaviour and leaves the 30 second cap in place. The cap is a deliberate fleet dispersal after a restart, main.ts line 3227. The reproduction knob SELFSYNC_E2E_RESTART_AT_LIVE guards the documented numbers: anyone can rerun them. No code path changed, so no new unit test. Pass 3, the rerun. 36 remote runs without an outage converge in 0.53 to 1.57 seconds, under 5 seconds. The slow path reproduces on demand with the knob: 13.51 seconds for a 10 second outage, 47.26 for 35. One finding: the fake transport in connect.test.ts called setEncrypted without the optional chain and failed tsc. Fixed in this sprint. No tracked Issue results. Verdict PASS.
    part e2eeRemoteLiveLatencyReviewGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "e1adbd59-8fda-4501-aa2a-e7918b55a6ed"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::proposed; :>> judgedAgainst = "be3f5ae"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-11-11"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
